A bit overpriced game but it is good. If you mix Far Cry 3, Far Cry 4, Mirror's Edge and some zombie game you will get Dying Light.
There are very strong cons:
1.The game constantly overwrites the settings file and even if you edit it always launches in a windowed mode, you have to reset it to the fullscreen mode every time. The other settings are reset too.
2. There are bugs that apparently will never be fixed. Multiplayer is full of 250 lvl people using the bug duplicating any endgame stuff and throwing it anywhere. This can spoil your experience.
3. I for some reason can't use shift+tab to call steam, capture in-steam screenshots , also can't switch between windows with ctrl+esc, only  ctrl+alt+del helps.
4. There is an idiotic thing I hate the most. The game uses system language as the chat language in co-op and if you want to type in english you have to change your system language to english and even in this case sometimes it will use the other language you have until you restart it. There is no way to switch the language in-game.
Compared to Far Cry 4:
-Slightly better inventory and crafting mechanic;
-Much worse weapon/weapon upgrade mechanic;
-Le parkour;
-Zombie setting;
-Multiplayer actually works;
-Much more bugs.

