Nice and cheap (on sale) "standalone DLC" for Titan Quest. I'm pretty sure this was made by the same devs that made TQ. Although I remember Iron Lore being dead for quite some time, I guess Crate is made of the guys from Iron Lore.
Anyway, this is much better than TQ remaster and the godawful DLC for TQ we got last year. What a horrible scam that was.
Yet it plays the same as TQ and has some of the same flaws pretty much (with a little better interface though).
+ there's more variety in gameplay compared to TQ;
+ graphics are just a little better but I'm pretty sure that the engine is the same;
+ game almost has no performance issues besides crashes (if you don't buy DLC);
+ very cheap when on sale and provides a good 20-30 hrs of gameplay before gets you bored, and you can still come back after some time to try other classes;
+ some interesting ideas rewarding exploration (keys, multi-level dungeons with bosses etc.);
+ quest choices, even though pretty simple ones. still good to have those;
+ I'm not sure if factions and reputation was a good idea, but it surely wasn't a bad one;
+ game crashed after the first cutscene of my first playthrough;
+ ok soundtrack;
+ ok weather system (for 2003 year graphics);
+ I have no idea why Crucible is a thing, but ok, good idea, I guess;
- extremely unbalanced (ranged playstyle and weaponry is way too easy and OP compared to melee), this was a thing in TQ as well though, Hunting was just so much easier than everything else pretty much, especially in remaster, when they broke camera zoom;
- has all the things I hated in TQ: lots undead and poison based enemies, boring skilltrees (except for devotion), huge unappealing levels with a mess of a color scheme so you can't see♥♥♥♥♥♥ 249 damage types and 454 resistance types (making some enemies easy and some one-shot you based on your gear) etc;
- additions for the sake of additions (like constant need to craft dynamite only to be able to open new areas which most of the time contain nothing of interest except some bosses), crafting materials you have to grind for and stuff;
- the story felt weak IMHO and main questline ended so fast I didn't even understand what happened, just ran out of the places to run to (probably didn't pay enough attention;
- DLC is as bad as it was in TQ: broken weapons (especially OP rifles, like OP spears in TQIT), ♥♥♥♥ing poison flowers you have to kill twice (yet again, game hates melees), DLC provides good FPS drops (which were absent in vanilla), DLC crashes on startup.
Overall, I can't say it's a bad game. I didn't expect much and I wasn't disappointed. This game never tried to be something bigger than it is. Just a full TQ clone in a new setting. I'm sure I didn't spend enough time on it yet, but I will get back to it eventually. Worth the summer/winter sale price for sure. DLC is total trash and really not worth it due to even worse balance and performance hits. Give it a try if you loved D2 or TQ.
Gave it a thumbs down only because I was unable to find a single bad review, so let it have a "bad" review that doesn't say the game is bad.

