Well, it's awesome that a gaming company invests in making this kinds of projects that only contributes to elevate the standards of one's gaming series. And just for the effort it deserves to be recommended, BUT...
-Amazingly fake guns;
-Rather terrible special effects;
-CRINGE acting (I'm looking at you agent Griffin);
-There were kids doing armed bodyguard roles... Some odd casting choices;
-Questionable dialogue choices;
-"Meh" action sequences;
Greta isn't in the game, but I think her and Gage performed the better. It's obvious low-budget, you can tell from miles away, but again, great effort!

